Callouts survive a face change; a Keys button in the header

Step 27 (inserted). Reported: callouts sometimes failed right after
changing faces. The stone's transform had CSS transitions (the settling
class after a turn, and always in read mode); the exact-anchor
measurement switches the transform off and back on each frame, and with
a transition active the switch-back animated, so the next frames' anchors
were computed mid-animation and every glyph seemed out of reach. The
transitions are gone (custom-property changes never animated anyway),
and the measurement also forces transition: none while it toggles.

Also reported: the key legend was not found. It has been in the Keys row
under the controls, with ? opening the full dialog; now a "Keys ?" button
sits beside the stone dropdown in the header and the lede says to rest
the pointer on anything and press ? for the keys. v=28 cache-busting.

